{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::graph` MUST expose the graph's associated types and content lookup operation:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Graph: Send + Sync {\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    /// The *contents* of a node defines what is given to a validator\n    /// when the node is read.\n    type NodeContent: Send + Sync;\n\n    /// The *label* between edges defines the kind of verification relationship\n    /// between two nodes.\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    /// User-defined errors that can occur when fetching node content or performing\n    /// other operations.\n    type Error: Send;\n\n    /// Fetch the content of a node.\n    fn node_content(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n\n    // ... additional methods defined below ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement is a signature contract. `habeas_sdk::graph::Graph` must expose four associated types, each with a stated bound set, and the `node_content` lookup. The trait is declared with `{impl}` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs#trait[Graph]`. The tests check it as follows.\n\n- **Trait and associated types are exposed.** Several marked tests implement the public `Graph` trait from outside the crate and set all four associated types. The implementers are `Memory` and `GraphWithChangingEdges` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs`, `Application` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs`, `Memory` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs`, and `StoredGraph` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs`. `HabeasDomain` implements it in `src/sdk.rs`. These implementations only compile if the trait exposes those types. The `Graph` trait itself is declared with the exact bounds the requirement lists (`NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`, `NodeContent: Send + Sync`, `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`, `Error: Send`).\n- **Bounds are no stricter than stated.** The tests use deliberately minimal types. The `Node` type in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` derives only `Clone`, `Eq` and `PartialEq`, and its comment says it has no Serde or Hash. The `Node` type in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs` has no `Hash` or `Display`. `EdgeLabel` is `()` or `u8`, and `NodeContent` is `()` in `StoredGraph`. A trait that demanded extra bounds on `NodeId` such as `Hash`, `Display` or `Serialize` would fail to compile against these implementers. Bounds that are looser than stated would break the SDK's own generic code, which relies on `Clone`, `Eq`, `Send` and `Sync`, and the SDK is compiled and exercised by every one of these tests.\n- **`node_content` returns `Result<NodeContent, Error>`.**\n  - In `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain]`, `graph.domain().node_content(&source).unwrap()` is compared with the expected delivered input and checked to contain `call();`. The same test shows an error result for a missing outline item (`inspection.read(&missing).is_err()`).\n  - In `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]`, `node_content` results are asserted through fingerprint equality and inequality.\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` and `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_have_independent_typed_answers_and_cache_negative_results]` read content through the validator and assert the dependency fingerprint. The latter asserts `state.reads.is_empty()`.\n  - `Error` is exercised with `io::Error`, `&'static str` and `FileStorageError`, so it is not tied to one type.\n\nI found no obligation in the text that lacks a test. The remaining behaviours in the cited tests, such as paths, caching and rendering, belong to other requirements and need no assessment here.",
  "references": "00e519cfbac0ed4a461c6b57cb38ac87dd66016f712a3da9e78788d6a7164538",
